{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918643-forsaken-hong-kong-brainstorming-ideas","id":918643,"title":"Forsaken Hong Kong - Brainstorming Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-21T08:49:42-07:00","id":918643,"title":"Forsaken Hong Kong - Brainstorming Ideas","content":"There is a moderate chance that I will be running a Forsaken game set in Hong Kong for my group in the near future.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor those familiar with Hong Kong, what features of the region, what bits of folklore, what cultural quirks are vital to take into account for a Werewolf game or would be great gaming fodder?<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about the famous cliches and tropes of HK known far and wide like triads and and the Walled City, but more the sorts of bits and pieces that aren't necessarily so well-known like 'Lion Rock spirit', villain hitting and similar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T10:23:36-07:00","id":918679,"title":"","content":"While not necessarily going to impact play, the practice of taking on an &quot;English&quot; or &quot;Christian&quot; name when dealing with foreigners leads to a lot of fun stuff; my mom used to do corporate jewelry work with a woman who called herself Pandora, and I read a police report about a man arrested by the name of Devil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 06-22-2016, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T11:02:52-07:00","id":918702,"title":"","content":"Hong Kong is a Lovely place. You need a separate visa for Hong Kong then from China, even though the British gave it back. Subways are common transport, as is bus and taxi. they have this thing called like an Octopus card or something that works on all the public transports. Signs are in English and Classic Chinese characters rather then simplified like the mainland. They have a massive wonderful nightmarket (Its worldfamous look it up) that you can get oodles of goods of various kinds from clothes, to flowers and electronics, and they have lots of cheap streetfood there.<br /> <br /> Many people speak English, but not everybody, some don't retain much from after highschool, it is generally easy enough to get around because many people there could possibly translate someone else for you. People that work at restaurants and hotels often speak excellent english. It has many western stores and businesses, like Seven Eleven, which is like a sooooothing Oasis for culture shocked individuals. Newstands often sell chinese translated manga which I found delightful. TV doesn't just show chinese programming it may have Korean shows, or a few in english.<br /> <br /> They have a beautiful Gardenpark with turtles and birds that tourists love. Look it up. It has a massive mall where you can see ships from the Harbor.<br /> I noticed electric outlets are not quite as omnipresent, for instance I could find none in the Airport, and I would have to use the Airports free Internet, but take a subway back to the Hotel every time I have to recharge. I also had to go on a rainy nightmarket jaunt to find an Adapter plug to translate my American plug to Hong Kong plugs. <br /> <br /> Hong Kong uses their own Currency different from China. The Island of Macau is close by and a lot of people go visit there as well. It is similar to Hong Kong but Portugal was the one that owned it.<br /> <br /> So lots of tourists, british, and foreigners of all kinds. And sometimes you can see monks collecting alms smiling and shaking hands at night in busy foottraffic. Foreigners are often easy to spot in a crowd because they are often taller, or wearing a backpack.<br /> <br /> Lovely place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T04:15:22-07:00","id":919636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918643-forsaken-hong-kong-brainstorming-ideas?p=918679#post918679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not necessarily going to impact play, the practice of taking on an &quot;English&quot; or &quot;Christian&quot; name when dealing with foreigners leads to a lot of fun stuff; my mom used to do corporate jewelry work with a woman who called herself Pandora, and I read a police report about a man arrested by the name of Devil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm aware of some of the interesting blending when it comes to names <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918643-forsaken-hong-kong-brainstorming-ideas?p=918702#post918702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*snip info*<br /> Lovely place.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, that's all fair enough - but less the sort of thing I'm looking for <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm looking for the stuff that makes meaty fodder for a Werewolf game set in the location.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T14:37:30-07:00","id":919942,"title":"","content":"Is this to be set during the present day? The last time I was in that neck of the world was the 80s, so I don't know how much things have changed since then. I might suggest Thailand and Singapoore as additional destinations to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12012-wayfinder","name":"Wayfinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T23:27:21-07:00","id":921371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/918643-forsaken-hong-kong-brainstorming-ideas#post918643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a moderate chance that I will be running a Forsaken game set in Hong Kong for my group in the near future.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor those familiar with Hong Kong, what features of the region, what bits of folklore, what cultural quirks are vital to take into account for a Werewolf game or would be great gaming fodder?<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about the famous cliches and tropes of HK known far and wide like triads and and the Walled City, but more the sorts of bits and pieces that aren't necessarily so well-known like 'Lion Rock spirit', villain hitting and similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feng Shui is a <b>huge</b> deal there. You won't see a business being set up, or built outright without a consultant on the spiritual energy flow.<br /> <br /> Beware an Idigam coalescing on such a concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T14:03:49-07:00","id":923471,"title":"","content":"So we had our setting and character creation session. There's some interesting stuff that I'll write up here at some point about the specifics of Uratha society in Hong Kong, and I've worked up an initial draft of details for the pack territory, history and non-werewolf members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T14:12:40-07:00","id":923477,"title":"","content":"Always cool seeing stuff from other peoples' games and you've obviously got a great grasp on Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-29-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T12:21:09-07:00","id":927733,"title":"","content":"The Kowloon Walled City probably still cast a shadow over the Hisil, as well. What did those walls built on human misery kept imprisoned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}